{"chunk_id": "3dbffda91cc2", "text": "Priests advise King Janamejaya to perform a divinely ordained \"snake\u2011sacrifice\" described in the Puranas to destroy Takshaka, the serpent responsible for his father\u2019s death. The king orders preparations, and a vast sacrificial platform is built according to Vedic rules. During construction, a learned builder ominously predicts that the ritual will ultimately be halted by a Brahmana, prompting the king to restrict entry to the ceremony. When the sacrifice begins, priests clad in black pour ghee into the sacred fire while chanting the names of serpents, magically drawing snakes from across the world into the flames. Multitudes\u2014of every size and color\u2014fall screaming into the fire, filling the air with smoke, stench, and terror. As the slaughter unfolds, Takshaka flees to Indra\u2019s palace seeking divine protection, setting up the coming intervention that may stop the catastrophic ritual.\nJanamejaya\u2019s snake-sacrifice begins; priests chant as countless serpents are drawn into the fire while Takshaka seeks refuge with Indra.\nThemes: vengeance ritual, sacrifice and destruction, fate and curse, divine refuge, Vedic ritual authority", "vector": [0.005217379424721003, -0.01573965698480606, -0.016655221581459045, 0.009236444719135761, -0.015941619873046875, 0.006678245961666107, -0.021771620959043503, -0.019065314903855324, 0.0062608555890619755, -0.01602240465581417, 0.004490312654525042, 0.003132110694423318, 0.011020451784133911, 0.011276272125542164, -0.012595764361321926, 0.0029755893629044294, 0.0454820841550827, -0.021933190524578094, 0.009626907296478748, -0.0030479594133794308, -0.01029338501393795, -0.0050760055892169476, 0.008960428647696972, 0.025662776082754135, -0.0187287088483572, 0.017234183847904205, -0.0054631014354527, -0.028705686330795288, 0.006543603725731373, 0.007169689517468214, -0.012979494407773018, -0.018822958692908287, -0.011814840137958527, 0.0004194941429886967, -0.033068086951